      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SPOILT ROTTEN (4) has been trying to win a race for some time, and again found one better when finishing second by just over a length here on a heavy track last week. He has a wide gate to cope with this time, but is still the one to beat. IT'S A LONG ROAD (2) rattled home too late here fresh up when finishing second by a short-head, and then got well out of his ground after being taken back from a wide gate at Ipswich last time out. He is better placed in this with a return to 1210m, and he is worth another chance, especially with the aid of a superior gate. PAINTED WINGS (7) ran the odd good race when trained in Victoria, and she should find the company in this area more to her liking. The nearly 6 weeks between runs would have done her no harm, and she is well worth a second glance if there is any market support for her. PROFFER (3) blew out late fresh up at Gatton, and he should be a lot harder to catch this time. Keep safe. LITTLE MISS CLASSY (6) has changed stables. Include.",
